module nysd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Southern District of New York's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"; the
// district's own computation rule, Local Criminal Rule 45.1, is
// withdrawn). The Local Criminal Rules apply listed Local Civil Rules in
// criminal proceedings (Local Criminal Rule 1.1(b)), among them Local
// Civil Rule 6.2 (orders on motions), 39.1 (custody of exhibits) and 72.1
// (powers of magistrate judges, also Local Criminal Rule 59.1(c)); the
// Local Civil Rules are not sectioned in the corpus, so none of their
// periods is encoded here. No trigger carries a service method: FRCrimP
// 45(c)'s three added days follow the manner of service (Local Criminal
// Rule 49.1(c): service under FRCrimP 49), which is not modeled here.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: a
// discovery or bill-of-particulars motion is heard only with counsel's
// good-faith conference affidavit (Local Criminal Rule 16.1); post-trial
// motions, including FRCrimP 34 and 35 motions, go to the trial judge
// (Local Criminal Rule 34.1), within the FRCrimP periods in lit/frcrimp;
// a represented defendant may not file pro se while the case is pending
// (Local Criminal Rule 49.2); and on a Criminal Rules Emergency the chief
// judge may issue orders not inconsistent with FRCrimP 62 (Local Criminal
// Rule 62.1).
//
// The earlier S.D.N.Y. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner v. United States,
// Brady v. Maryland and the others it named) are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial
// Act or constitutional authority and belong to lit/frcrimp; they are
// removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// The memorandum accompanying a motion for reconsideration: at most 10
/// pages (Local Criminal Rule 49.1(b)).
limit reconsideration-memorandum {
  pages <= 10 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(b)"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(b)"

/// A reply memorandum on a motion for reconsideration: at most 5 pages; an
/// answering memorandum is at most 10 (Local Criminal Rule 49.1(b)).
limit reconsideration-reply {
  pages <= 5 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(b)"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(b)"

/// The information a party's FRCrimP 12.4 disclosure statement requires
/// changes (Local Criminal Rule 12.4).
event DisclosureInformationChanged()
/// The date set for trial (Local Criminal Rule 16.2).
event TrialScheduled()
/// Motion papers are served (Local Criminal Rule 49.1(a)(1)).
event MotionServed()
/// Opposing papers are served (Local Criminal Rule 49.1(a)(2)).
event OppositionServed()
/// The court determines a motion (Local Criminal Rule 49.1(b)).
event MotionDetermined()
/// A motion for reconsideration is filed with its memorandum (Local
/// Criminal Rule 49.1(b)).
event ReconsiderationFiled() paper reconsideration-memorandum
/// A reply memorandum on reconsideration is filed (Local Criminal Rule
/// 49.1(b)).
event ReconsiderationReplyFiled() paper reconsideration-reply

/// Local Criminal Rule 12.4: for FRCrimP 12.4(b)(2), "promptly" means
/// within 14 days: a supplemental disclosure statement is filed within 14
/// days of any change in the information the statement requires.
deadline supplemental-disclosure-statement: 14.days after DisclosureInformationChanged() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 12.4"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Local Criminal Rule 16.2: unless the court orders otherwise, the
/// government makes its FRCrimP 16(a)(1)(G) expert disclosures at least 60
/// days before trial.
deadline government-expert-disclosure: 60.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 16.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Local Criminal Rule 16.2: unless the court orders otherwise, the defense
/// makes its expert disclosures at least 30 days before trial.
deadline defense-expert-disclosure: 30.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 16.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Local Criminal Rule 49.1(a)(1): unless a statute or rule provides
/// otherwise or the court orders otherwise in a judge's individual
/// practices or in the case, opposing papers are filed within 14 days after
/// service of the motion papers.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Local Criminal Rule 49.1(a)(2): reply papers are filed within seven days
/// after service of the opposing papers, unless the court orders
/// otherwise.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after OppositionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// Local Criminal Rule 49.1(b): a motion for reconsideration of an order
/// determining a motion is filed within 14 days after the court's
/// determination of the original motion.
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after MotionDetermined() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Crim. R. 49.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
